{
  "families": [
    {
      "budget_share": 45,
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 14, "param": "data_width"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 22, "low": 10, "param": "n_iter"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"},
        {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"}
      ],
      "why": "Fully pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput equals Fmax and the 50 MSPS constraint is easy; this family anchors the high-throughput end of the front. data_width >= 14 and n_iter >= 10 are needed to reach the 2^-12 error bound, while the guard/rounding knobs let the search trade area/power against accuracy."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 55,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 14, "param": "data_width"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 22, "low": 10, "param": "n_iter"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"},
        {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
        {"choices": null, "high": 8, "low": 2, "param": "m"}
      ],
      "why": "Registering every m stages cuts the flip-flop count versus full pipelining, which should lower the power index; the longer combinational path lowers Fmax but 50 MSPS leaves ample headroom. Same accuracy knobs as pipelined, so this family should supply the low-power end of the Pareto front."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Both allowed families are 1-result/cycle, so the 50 MSPS throughput constraint is satisfied as long as Fmax >= 50 MHz, which is very likely for these short CORDIC datapaths. Accuracy depends only on data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard and rounding, so I search the same accuracy box in both families and let the register structure (full vs every-m-stage) drive the power trade-off. data_width is bounded below at 14 because the output LSB is 2^-(W-2) and the spec needs max_abs_err <= 2^-12; n_iter starts at 10 to allow convergence. The full guard/rounding ranges are kept open because they are cheap ways to buy accuracy without widening the datapath. Budget is split slightly toward pipelined_m since it is the more likely low-power candidate for the min-power selection rule, while pipelined still maps the high-throughput/high-power corner."
}
